// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// rules/shared/ - code the rules share. Copy this file, rename it, and delete this header.
//
//   Name it after what it holds - `ItemTypes.cs`, `Refs.cs`, `Naming.cs`. **No `Rules` suffix**,
//   because nothing here is a rule: this folder is compiled into every rule and executed on its
//   own never.
//
//   Rename to `.cs`. A `.template` file is not scanned, which is the only reason this one can sit
//   here without being compiled into every rule.
//
// What it is for   Constants a project keeps in one place, small helpers several rules call, and
//                  the item-type numbers that would otherwise be repeated in twenty files.
//
// No entry point   A file here has no `Validate` method. One that does is still not run - the
//                  folder decides, not the shape of the file.
//
// Taking a context  A helper that reports takes the narrowest context it actually uses, and the
//                  four nest: IPreContext, then IGlobalContext, then ITableContext and
//                  IRuntimeContext beside each other. A helper taking IGlobalContext can be
//                  called from the table, global and runtime stages alike.
//
// Unlike the rule folders, **this one is scanned all the way down**: subfolders are somebody
// organising their helpers rather than a rule with no stage.
//
// One thing to know: each rule file is its own compilation, so `static` state declared here is
// per rule rather than shared between them. That is deliberate - it is what lets the table rules
// run at the same time without racing each other.
//
// Full guide: doc/validation.md
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

